From 06c907fffd6691d3745d25c5c96f6e6fbaec89be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 18:21:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] controller: bound station churn and honor cross-band
 ownership

Rapid station moves exposed three related defects. Every association event
cloned a multi-megabyte empty data model for each orchestration stage,
cross-radio non-MLO evidence could be suppressed, and an ordinary non-MLO
disassociation was ignored when no Associated STA MLD record existed. A
transient 2.4-to-5 GHz association could consequently consume hundreds of
MiB and leave the controller showing the obsolete BSS.

Keep station-event stages lightweight, preserve cross-radio non-MLO ownership
evidence in agent snapshots, and apply non-MLO withdrawals directly to the
controller maps. Add focused tests for lightweight stage cloning and normal
station withdrawal.

Upstream-Status: Pending
